  "id": "Compound::DB05271 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Rotigotine is implicated in the pathogenesis of Lipoedema and Stereotypy, both of which are linked to Mirabegron and Dexmethylphenidate, respectively. These compounds bind to Cyp2d6, a cytochrome P450 enzyme, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Rotigotine may influence Cyp2d6 activity. The shared pathway involves the interaction of Rotigotine with a common ancestor, an Organic Aromatic Compound or an Agent Affecting Nervous System, which links it to Mirabegron and Dexmethylphenidate. This suggests that Rotigotine may modulate Cyp2d6 through a common biochemical pathway, possibly by affecting the activity of the enzyme or by influencing its expression. The evidence supports a potential role for Rotigotine in regulating Cyp2d6, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
